1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,949
In 1838, a militia marched more than 800

2
00:00:03,959 --> 00:00:06,475
Potawatomi out of Indiana at gunpoint.

3
00:00:06,705 --> 00:00:08,648
It started at Twin Lakes, near Plymouth.

4
00:00:09,298 --> 00:00:11,945
Their leader, Menominee, had refused to

5
00:00:11,955 --> 00:00:13,205
give up his people's land.

6
00:00:13,435 --> 00:00:15,745
So the governor sent General John Tipton

7
00:00:15,755 --> 00:00:17,315
and a volunteer militia.

8
00:00:17,765 --> 00:00:19,857
On September 4, the march began.

9
00:00:20,087 --> 00:00:22,299
Menominee and two other leaders were held

10
00:00:22,309 --> 00:00:23,704
under guard in a wagon.

11
00:00:23,934 --> 00:00:26,270
The militia burned the village so no one

12
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:26,917
could return.

13
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:30,988
They traveled about 660 miles, to what is

14
00:00:30,998 --> 00:00:32,081
now eastern Kansas.

15
00:00:32,311 --> 00:00:33,418
It took 2 months.

16
00:00:33,868 --> 00:00:36,525
At least 42 people died on the way, many

17
00:00:36,535 --> 00:00:37,375
of them children.

18
00:00:37,605 --> 00:00:39,647
It became known as the Trail of Death.

19
00:00:40,497 --> 00:00:42,886
Today, markers follow the route across 4

20
00:00:42,896 --> 00:00:43,333
states.

21
00:00:43,563 --> 00:00:46,238
And near Twin Lakes, a statue of Menominee

22
00:00:46,248 --> 00:00:47,804
has stood since 1909.

23
00:00:48,354 --> 00:00:50,516
Comment your town for the next La Porte

24
00:00:50,526 --> 00:00:51,257
After Dark.

